# CiDispatchStalled, lifted VERBATIM out of prometheusrule.yaml — the rules file that
# queued-age.promtool-test loads. Not a manifest and not applied to anything: `promtool test
# rules` needs upstream-format rules (top-level `groups:`), and a PrometheusRule keeps them under
# `.spec`, so the CR cannot be loaded directly. Named .promtool-rules rather than .yaml on
# purpose — manifest-lint kubeconforms EVERY *.yaml under argocd/resources and a non-manifest
# there would fail it.
#
# THE COPY CANNOT DRIFT SILENTLY: `devbox run exporter-self-test` (gated in CI) reads the alert
# out of both files and asserts expr/for/labels are identical. homelab#288 (FU-158) owns the
# harness that will extract `.spec.groups` at run time and delete the copy altogether; this file
# is what makes the fixture runnable in the meantime.
#
# Regenerate after editing the alert in prometheusrule.yaml:
#   yq '{"groups": [{"name": "github", "rules": [.spec.groups[].rules[] | select(.alert == "CiDispatchStalled")]}]}' \
#     argocd/resources/github-exporter/prometheusrule.yaml
groups:
  - name: github
    rules:
      - alert: CiDispatchStalled
        expr: max by (owner, runner) (time() - github_workflow_run_queued_since_timestamp{runner!="hosted"}) > 1800
        for: 10m
        labels:
          severity: warning
          platform_machinery: "true"
        annotations:
          summary: "CI cannot dispatch: {{ $labels.runner }} runs queued {{ $value | humanizeDuration }}"
          description: 'The oldest {{ $labels.runner }} workflow run in {{ $labels.owner }} has waited {{ $value | humanizeDuration }} for a runner (normal pickup ~20s). A queued run never fails, so no CI-failure alert can see this. Which runs: github_workflow_run_queued_since_timestamp{runner!="hosted"}. Check in this order: (1) githubstatus.com / GithubVendorOutage — vendor-side, and do NOT re-run queued work; (2) saturation vs breakage — a saturated pool has jobs RUNNING, a broken one has workers WAITING (maxRunners is 4, argocd/platform/arc-runners.yaml); (3) kubectl -n arc-runners get pods,ephemeralrunnersets,autoscalinglisteners, then the LISTENER POD''s own log — the 2026-08-07 wedge (docs/incidents/2026-08-07-arc-listener-wedge.md) was visible ONLY there; (4) WAN reachability from each runner node — 2026-08-11 (docs/incidents/2026-08-11-wk-metal-02-default-route-loss.md) was one node''s missing default route with the listener healthy.'
